 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Image-Based NeRF Training
-Training a NeRF using RGB images as ground truth, optimizing both geometry (via Eikonal loss) and appearance (via color loss) [S3, unofficial]. It involves loading datasets using `get_nerf_datasets`, sampling random pixels to construct ray bundles, and computing color loss as mean squared error [S3, unofficial]. Eikonal loss is added for geometry regularization, similar to SDF training [S3, unofficial]. The learning rate is updated using a scheduler after each epoch [S3, unofficial]. This variant typically runs for 250 epochs on 128x128 images for datasets like lego [S3, unofficial].
+Trains a NeRF using RGB images as ground truth, optimizing both geometry (via Eikonal loss) and appearance (via color loss) [S3, unofficial]. It differs from the main setup by explicitly adding Eikonal loss for geometry regularization and running for a fixed number of epochs (250) on smaller images ($128 \times 128$) [S3, unofficial]. Choose this when geometry regularization is critical for the scene structure [S3, unofficial].
 
