 ## Background
-The method originates from the Control-NeRF paper, which introduces editable feature volumes for scene rendering and manipulation [S1]. It builds on the standard NeRF framework but replaces positional encoding of 3D positions with sampled feature vectors [S1]. The use of Nerfstudio, NerfAcc, and Instant-NGP for fast convergence is detailed in research on abdominal 3-D scene rendering from laparoscopy surgical videos [S2]. The Image-Based NeRF Training variant is described in an unofficial assignment repository [S3, unofficial].
+
+*   **Origin:** Control-NeRF was introduced in 2022 [S1]. The use of Nerfstudio, NerfAcc, and Instant-NGP for surgical video rendering was described in 2023 [S2].
+*   **History:** Developed to enable editable scene representations and fast training for specific applications like laparoscopic surgery [S1, S2].
+*   **Usage:** Used in medical imaging for abdominal 3-D scene rendering from laparoscopy videos [S2].
 
